[00:16.76]When I think of you
[00:23.16]I close my eyes, filled with longing
[00:30.16]I have had so many things
[00:36.40]Everything but happiness
[00:46.32]My long fingers run
[00:52.32]Through sad verses I invent
[01:00.04]Not even what I devote myself to
[01:06.72]Brings me any contentment now
[01:10.16]It may even be morning
[01:13.52]Early, bright as the day
[01:16.92]But nothing that they tell me
[01:21.12]Makes me feel any joy
[01:23.28]I only wanted, from the wild
[01:26.76]A taste of raspberries
[01:29.68]So I could run among the flowerbeds
[01:33.36]And hide my sorrow
[01:36.16]I am still too young for so much sorrow
[01:39.00]Let us stop all this and tend to life
[01:42.68]Or else death, or something like it, will come
[01:46.12]And sweep us away, young man, before we have lived
